{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"poisonous-lowly-anole","creation_channel":"python","description":"Remove the refs that pin pre-rewrite history, and take a backup that lives outside the repo.\nWithout this the reclaim lands at **167 MB instead of ~94 MiB**. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Why\nMeasured: remote tag `pre-heal-a118-20260710T005736Z` (`2a77dd48`) is an ancestor of\n`origin/tickets` and pins **22,317 commits / 63,202,159 bytes** of `.bridge_state`. A full clone\nfetches tags, so leaving it defeats most of the reclaim. It is absent from Gerrit and replication is\n`mirror = false`, so deletion sticks and will not be recreated. Also delete the host-local\n`pre-a3-remediation` tag (`0adbd40a`, ~64.8 MB reachable).\n\nAn **in-repo** archive branch or tag reclaims nothing — reachable objects are served and repacked\nforever (crates.io's receipts: 1.73 GB live index vs **6.94 GB** archive repo). So the backup must\nleave the repository: `git bundle create` from an **unfiltered** clone, stored off-repo, including the\ntag tips being deleted.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `git ls-remote --heads --tags origin` (de-peeling `^{}` entries) is enumerated at run time and\n      every ref whose ancestry intersects the old tip is listed. Do **not** hardcode a count — today\n      it is 13 heads + 16 distinct tags. Tier: **repo-level script**.\n- [ ] After deletion, **no ref a default clone fetches** has the old tip as an ancestor. Tier:\n      `ls-remote` + `merge-base --is-ancestor` loop. (Scoped deliberately: origin also carries ~120\n      `refs/pull/*` and ~2,671 `refs/changes/*`, but those descend from `main`'s root and a default\n      clone fetches neither. `refs/reconciler/lock` is a **blob**, so it carries no ancestry.)\n- [ ] The off-repo bundle exists, was created from an **unfiltered** clone, contains the old tip and\n      both deleted tag tips, and `git bundle verify` passes. **[operator-attested]**\n- [ ] Restoring the bundle into a scratch repo reproduces the old tip SHA exactly. Tier:\n      **integration** in a throwaway clone.\n\n## Files\n`infra/scripts/` (hygiene + bundle helper), runbook notes\n\nScope: S. Depends on A6-0c (the bundle should be taken with the same unfiltered-clone helper).","id":"dbaa-0c96-0e01-4238","parent_id":"81fa-bbe5-3067-4865","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"A6-0d: pre-window ref hygiene and off-repo backup bundle"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788222658256588001,"uuid":"40553ab5-c3a3-446d-a967-2c5b08aadb57"}